      budget: 9
      level: 1
      group: openrouter

    # .note = this lane grades the SURFACES a human meets — the cli entrypoints, the
    #         renderers, the skill wrappers, and the snapshots that pin what they print.
    #         so it KEEPS every __snapshots__ file (its evidence) and KEEPS the wish,
    #         vision, and execution yields (where an accepted friction is declared, and
    #         where this lane's own prior blockers named their remedy).
    #
    #         🔴 that last is why `.behavior/**` is NOT shed wholesale here, as it is on
    #         five peer lanes: this lane's remedy lives in the yield, so a bind that hid
    #         the yield would make it re-raise the same concern forever.
    #
    #         what it sheds: the journey BODIES (*.test.ts — the snapshots beside them
    #         carry the rendered surface), and the route's design-fork and wisher-quote
    #         records, which are 11.1% of the corpus and hold no surface a human reads.
    #
    #         it also sheds the LATER stones' yields (`5.3.*` and on): at i003 the lane
    #         overflowed at 76.2% (469k tokens), and `5.3.verification.yield.md` alone was
    #         33.2k of it — a record this stone does not produce. the 5.1 yield stays.
    #
    # 🔴 NARROWED 2026-09-26, after it overflowed at i005 (78.3%, 208 files, 452.2k
    #    target tokens), read from that run's own `tokens.expected.md`:
    #      .agent/                          41.7k  9.2%  glossary clusters + briefs
    #      compileReviewPrompt*.snap        42.2k  9.3%  the prompt sent to the BRAIN
    #    neither is a surface a human meets at the cli, so both leave (~84k, to ~70%).
    #    the cli snapshots, renderers, and the 5.1 yield all stay.
    - slug: ergo-friction-hazards
      run: $rhx review --repo bhrain --mode hard --brain openrouter/deepseek/flash --rules '.agent/repo=bhuild/role=behaver/briefs/practices/behavior.execution/architect/rule.forbid.friction-hazards.md' --refs '.agent/repo=ehmpathy/role=ergonomist/briefs/*.md' --refs '.agent/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/briefs/practices/lang.tones/*.md.min' --refs '.agent/repo=bhuild/role=behaver/briefs/practices/behavior.verification/*.md' --diffs since-main --paths-with '**/*.{ts,sh,md,snap}' --paths-without '**/*.test.ts' --paths-without '.behavior/**/.fulcrums/**' --paths-without '.behavior/**/.seeds/**' --paths-without '.behavior/**/5.3.*' --paths-without '.agent/**' --paths-without '.scratch/**' --paths-without '**/__snapshots__/compileReviewPrompt.*.snap' --paths-without 'src/domain.operations/review/**' --paths-without 'src/domain.operations/route/**' --join intersect --conversation $conversation --output "$output"
      budget: 16
      level: 1
      group: openrouter

    # .note = the route twin of the lane above (see `.SPLIT 2026-10-07` on
    #         `behavior-intent-coverage`): the route subtree's renderers and the snapshots
    #         that pin what they print, under the same rules, refs, and excludes
    - slug: ergo-friction-hazards-route
